Wolmar is the name of the southern end of the long beach at Flic en Flac. The sand and the lagoon are the same as in the village centre but the atmosphere is calmer: larger hotels line part of the shore and there are fewer crowds even at weekends.

Looking south along the coast you see the mountains above Tamarin and on clear days Le Morne in the distance. The beach faces west so the evenings here are as good as anywhere on the coast.

## Good to know

- Access to the sand is public; use the public paths and car parks rather than hotel grounds.
- The lagoon is calm inside the reef; do not swim out towards the reef or the passes.
